OL,3,GNEWSA'As soon as I work, I get         
OL,4,Apenalised - I fear I will never own my 
OL,5,Aown home'                              
OL,7,FA disabled man fears he will never be  
OL,8,Fable to own his own home because of    
OL,9,Flimits on how much he can save due to  
OL,10,Fsocial care rules.                     
OL,12,FMaxwell McKnight, from St Neots, has   
OL,13,Fspinal muscular atrophy and receives   
OL,14,Fdirect payments from Cambridgeshire    
OL,15,FCounty Council for his care.           
OL,17,FHe works full-time in a graduate-level 
OL,18,Fjob and is saving for a house deposit. 
OL,19,FHowever, the adult social care upper   
OL,20,Fcapital limit is #23,250, meaning      
OL,21,Fanything he manages to save above that 
OL,22,Flimit will go towards his care instead.
OL,23,APub: 23-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
